Linear Algebra for Everyone
Gilbert Strang, Massachusetts Institue of Technology, Cambridge, MA
This book by Gilbert Strang, author of the widely-used Introduction to Linear Algebra, presents a “new start” in teaching and learning linear algebra, a subject that is increasingly important in all quantitative disciplines. Working with small matrices of integers, students can see dependent columns and the rank of A and its column space. This is a big step toward the four fundamental subspaces — a widespread success in teaching linear algebra. The new start makes linear algebra more approachable to students with a wide range of backgrounds. The text features many illustrative examples and exercises, and video lectures to accompany the book are available via MIT OpenCourseWare. The author’s site contains additional sample material and an instructor’s manual.
